---
code: K0002
title: Unexpected Character
description: "Encountered an invalid or unrecognized character during lexing"
severity: ERROR
since: 0.1.0
category: parse
tags: [parse, lexer, token]
deprecated: False
---

The lexer encountered a character that is not valid in Kura source code outside of a string literal or comment—such as non-ASCII punctuation, smart quotes (`“` or `”`), or unsupported symbolic operators.

## Example

```kura
let count = 10 § 2
```

Remove the unrecognized character or replace it with a valid Kura operator (such as [`*`]{.expected}, [`+`]{.expected}, [`/`]{.expected}, or [`%`]{.expected}):

```kura
let count = 10 * 2
```

::: note
If you intended to include arbitrary Unicode characters as text, place them inside double quotes (`"..."`). See the [EBNF](https://s0cks.github.io/kura) for valid lexical tokens.
:::
